came to pass, that when the gates of Jerusalem began to be dark before the sabbath, I commanded that the gates should be shut, and charged that they should not be opened till after the sabbath: and some of my servants set I at the gates, that there should no burden be brought in on the sabbath day.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙXSo the merchants and sellers of all kind of ware lodged without Jerusalem once or twice.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ²Then I testified against them, and said unto them, Why lodge ye about the wall? if ye do so again, I will lay hands on you. From that time forth came they no more on the sabbath.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙîAnd I commanded the Levites that they should cleanse themselves, and that they should come and keep the gates, to sanctify the sabbath day. Remember me, O my God, concerning this also, and spare me according to the greatness of thy mercy.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙVIn those days also saw I Jews that had married wives of Ashdod, of Ammon, and of Moab:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙand their children spake half in the speech of Ashdod, and could not speak in the Jews' language, but according to the language of each people.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙôAnd I contended with them, and cursed them, and smote certain of them, and plucked off their hair, and made them swear by God, saying, Ye shall not give your daughters unto their sons, nor take their daughters unto your sons, or for yourselves.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙâDid not Solomon king of Israel sin by these things? yet among many nations was there no king like him, who was beloved of his God, and God made him king over all Israel: nevertheless even him did outlandish women cause to sin.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrShall we then hearken unto you to do all this great evil, to transgress against our God in marrying strange wives?¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd one of the sons of Joiada, the son of Eliashib the high priest, was son in law to Sanballat the Horonite: therefore I chased him from me.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙzRemember them, O my God, because they have defiled the priesthood, and the covenant of the priesthood, and of the Levites.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ{Thus cleansed I them from all strangers, and appointed the wards of the priests and the Levites, every one in his business;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙhand for the wood offering, at times appointed, and for the firstfruits. Remember me, O my God, for good.¦layout ªlast_verse